<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urnayr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urnayr was a king of Caucasian Albania in the 4th century, remembered as the ruler who made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> the religion of his kingdom. Albanian and Armenian tradition links his baptism to the mission of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-the-illuminator">Gregory the Illuminator</a>. He is known mainly from the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/history-of-the-country-of-albania">History of the Country of Albania</a> attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movses-kaghankatvatsi">Movses Kaghankatvatsi</a>.</p></div>
